# Each ignore needs a reason. Keep this list short.

# AVD-AWS-0107 / AVD-AWS-0104: the web security group intentionally allows 80/443 from the internet
# (it is a public website) and egress to 80/443 for package repos. SSH is closed by default.
AVD-AWS-0107
AVD-AWS-0104

# AVD-AWS-0178: VPC flow logs are optional (enable_flow_logs) to avoid CloudWatch cost on a dev budget.
AVD-AWS-0178

# AWS-0132: the Terraform state bucket uses SSE-S3 (AES256) rather than a customer-managed KMS key.
# A CMK is about $1/month and adds little for a single-owner state bucket; revisit for a team setup.
AWS-0132

# AWS-0053: the ALB is internet-facing on purpose; it is the public entry point of the site.
AWS-0053
# AWS-0054: port 80 forwards plain HTTP only when no domain is configured (ACM cannot issue a
# certificate without one). With domain_name set, port 80 only redirects to HTTPS.
AWS-0054
# AWS-0095: the alarm topic is unencrypted because CloudWatch cannot publish to a topic that uses the
# AWS-managed SNS key, and a customer-managed key costs extra.
AWS-0095

# AWS-0177: RDS deletion protection is off so a budget demo can be torn down with `terraform destroy`.
# Turn it on (deletion_protection = true) for any environment that holds real data.
AWS-0177
